{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-036",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 36,
  "title": "Job 36",
  "display_title": "Job 36",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 36,
  "sortOrder": 18036,
  "verseCount": 33,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Elihu also proceeded, and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Suffer me a little, and I will shew thee that I have yet to speak on God’s behalf.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "I will fetch my knowledge from afar, and will ascribe righteousness to my Maker.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "For truly my words shall not be false: he that is perfect in knowledge is with thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Behold, God is mighty, and despiseth not any: he is mighty in strength and wisdom.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "He preserveth not the life of the wicked: but giveth right to the poor.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "He withdraweth not his eyes from the righteous: but with kings are they on the throne; yea, he doth establish them for ever, and they are exalted.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "And if they be bound in fetters, and be holden in cords of affliction;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Then he sheweth them their work, and their transgressions that they have exceeded.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "He openeth also their ear to discipline, and commandeth that they return from iniquity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "If they obey and serve him, they shall spend their days in prosperity, and their years in pleasures.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "But if they obey not, they shall perish by the sword, and they shall die without knowledge.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "But the hypocrites in heart heap up wrath: they cry not when he bindeth them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "They die in youth, and their life is among the unclean.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "He delivereth the poor in his affliction, and openeth their ears in oppression.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Even so would he have removed thee out of the strait into a broad place, where there is no straitness; and that which should be set on thy table should be full of fatness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "But thou hast fulfilled the judgment of the wicked: judgment and justice take hold on thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Because there is wrath, beware lest he take thee away with his stroke: then a great ransom cannot deliver thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Will he esteem thy riches? no, not gold, nor all the forces of strength.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Desire not the night, when people are cut off in their place.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Take heed, regard not iniquity: for this hast thou chosen rather than affliction.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Behold, God exalteth by his power: who teacheth like him?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Who hath enjoined him his way? or who can say, Thou hast wrought iniquity?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Remember that thou magnify his work, which men behold.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "Every man may see it; man may behold it afar off.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "Behold, God is great, and we know him not, neither can the number of his years be searched out.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "For he maketh small the drops of water: they pour down rain according to the vapour thereof:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "Which the clouds do drop and distil upon man abundantly.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "Also can any understand the spreadings of the clouds, or the noise of his tabernacle?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "Behold, he spreadeth his light upon it, and covereth the bottom of the sea.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "For by them judgeth he the people; he giveth meat in abundance.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "With clouds he covereth the light; and commandeth it not to shine by the cloud that cometh betwixt.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:36:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "The noise thereof sheweth concerning it, the cattle also concerning the vapour.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 36:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:36:33"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
